{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He shall not touch it.</b> The word \"it\" [בו] refers to the person who touches the mountain. The meaning: no other person may enter after him to seize him; rather, those who see him from their standing place shall stone him at once, and if he is far off, they shall shoot him with arrows." "<b>And the word יירה.</b> It is irregular, for the rule of roots with yod is that they interchange with vav in the nif'al future, like ולא יִוָדַע השבע (Genesis 41:31), יסרתני וָאִוָסֵר (Jeremiah 31:17). Perhaps they did so lest it pattern with למען <b>תורא</b> (Psalms 100:3), for alef and heh are quiescent at the end of a word; there is no difference between them in pronunciation." "<b>Whether beast or man, it shall not live.</b> And not birds, for they cannot be caught since it flies away at once." "<b>When the ram's horn sounds.</b> It means a ram [כבש], and it is called yovel on account of והעברת שופר תרועה (Leviticus 25:9), for a shofar is from the horn of a ram. And so it is written: במשוך בקרן היובל בשמעכם את קול השופר (Joshua 6:5). And it is astonishing what they say — that on account of וקול השופר הולך וחזק מאד, Moses speaks of the drawing of the yovel — for the sound of the shofar is a great wonder; there is nothing greater than it at the standing at Mount Sinai, for sounds and lightning and a heavy cloud are also seen in the world, but the sound of the shofar was never heard until the day of the Ten Commandments, and behold it was not from a ram's horn." "Said the Gaon [Saadia]: when Moses blows the shofar, then he gives them permission to ascend, and this was after Moses descended on the Day of Atonement, and he commanded to make the Tabernacle." "<b>They shall ascend the mountain.</b> Said R. Samuel ben Hofni: the meaning of \"they\" is Aaron and his sons and the seventy elders, concerning whom it is written: ואל משה אמר עלה את ה' אתה ואהרן נדב ואביהוא ושבעים מזקני ישראל (Exodus 24:1). And to the rest of Israel he gave no permission to ascend Mount Sinai; therefore he said \"they\" and not others. And his words are good in my eyes, for the Glory was always upon the mountain until the Tabernacle was made, as it is written: וכבוד ה' מלא את המשכן (Exodus 40:34). Then He spoke with Moses in the Tent of Meeting. Perhaps then Moses blew the shofar and gave permission to ascend when the Glory departed."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {5 "Ibn Ezra cites Exodus 40:34 as 'מ לד' which appears to be a corrupted abbreviation for chapter 40 verse 34; resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:02.324342387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}